The class `InnerQueuedObserver` is a thin coordination component whose performance is tightly coupled with the surrounding RxJava infrastructure (parent observer, queues, disposables, fusion modes). Its methods mainly delegate to other objects or perform trivial state updates, making isolated micro‑benchmarks of little value. Meaningful performance measurement should be done at a higher level (e.g., benchmarking whole reactive pipelines) rather than targeting this internal helper directly. Hence, generating a JMH benchmark for this class is unnecessary.